Backport of https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kueue/pull/16742 at commit
b28eeae (open upstream): an elastic Workload scaled down below its minCount
fails validation.

With partial scale-up, Kueue sets a worker group's minCount to the count the
job was created with. A later scale-down lowered count in place but kept
minCount, which the API server rejects with "minCount should be less or equal
to count". The scale-down now caps minCount at the new count, the Workload
webhook accepts exactly that cap, and a Workload that has never held quota
takes minCount from the job again, so its first admission stays
all-or-nothing. The PR's KEP text and end-to-end test are not included.

